(4679594, 673977, 60495, '<td valign="top">The buliding and the trees have a nice foggy sepia tone which is nice but the tree limbs hanging down look out of place and really do not look like they fit in the scene.</td>', 'The buliding and the trees have a nice foggy sepia tone which is nice but the tree limbs hanging down look out of place and really do not look like they fit in the scene.', '2008-05-04 16:55:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(4679596, 674348, 65037, '<td valign="top">It is great how the entertainer is sharp.  The lines of his arms and the direction of his gaze pull the eye to the sphere.  The background  distracts from the strength of the image, though.  You were probably limited in adjusting lighting and angle, but shallower depth of field might have helped blur the background so as not to be as distracting.</td>', 'It is great how the entertainer is sharp.  The lines of his arms and the direction of his gaze pull the eye to the sphere.  The background  distracts from the strength of the image, though.  You were probably limited in adjusting lighting and angle, but shallower depth of field might have helped blur the background so as not to be as distracting.', '2008-05-04 16:59:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(4679605, 674426, 60495, '<td valign="top">She should know better than jumping on the bed:) The lighting for the shot just does not do her justice, A little more lighting on the face would be nice and getting rid of the shadows behind her head by adding background light to light the wall behind her may have helped.</td>', 'She should know better than jumping on the bed:) The lighting for the shot just does not do her justice, A little more lighting on the face would be nice and getting rid of the shadows behind her head by adding background light to light the wall behind her may have helped.', '2008-05-04 17:03:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(4679607, 672895, 65037, '<td valign="top">great to catch the owl -- just wish he were sharper</td>', 'great to catch the owl -- just wish he were sharper', '2008-05-04 17:04:45.000000', NULL, 1),
