(4689760, 672970, 70661, '<td valign="top">Awesome! Many congrats!</td>', 'Awesome! Many congrats!', '2008-05-08 08:12:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(4689803, 673922, 89341, '<td valign="top">As per your feedback request ....<br/>The tight crop bothers me a little, I''m not sure the sepia conversion really adds anything to the photo (for me) a larger tonal range seems to be better.<br/>Maybe a wider angle with some trees may have helped.<br/>I guess sepia should have a softer feel to it but personally I like this a little better with approx 50% @ 1px USM applied.<br/>I didn''t vote in this challenge but if I had I''d be giving you a 6.</td>', 'As per your feedback request ....The tight crop bothers me a little, I''m not sure the sepia conversion really adds anything to the photo (for me) a larger tonal range seems to be better.Maybe a wider angle with some trees may have helped.I guess sepia should have a softer feel to it but personally I like this a little better with approx 50% @ 1px USM applied.I didn''t vote in this challenge but if I had I''d be giving you a 6.', '2008-05-08 08:40:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(4689810, 673922, 47906, '<td valign="top">I didnt vote in this challenge, there is some nice textures to the shot but the overall hue isnt a sepia color IMO, There is not tonal range or much contrast to it. It also  feels very cramped inside the space. <br/> <br/>Hope this helps.<br/></td>', 'I didnt vote in this challenge, there is some nice textures to the shot but the overall hue isnt a sepia color IMO, There is not tonal range or much contrast to it. It also  feels very cramped inside the space.  Hope this helps.', '2008-05-08 08:44:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(4689829, 673922, 39850, '<td valign="top">In response to your <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=775438" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">request</a> for comments.<br/> <br/>I gave this a 4.  Quite a nice capture with her eyes and the mane / hair blowing in the wind.  Depending what you had to work with, perhaps a variation in cropping, including a nudge rotate up on the right to straighten.  The centered composition isn''t as strong as something off-centered may have been in my opinion, but again, depends what you had to work with.  The tone itself perhaps a little strong (especially on the pink side) but that could be intentional.  A variation in the hue/tone may have brought out more features as well.  Overall the focus seems a bit soft, but could be a result of the pp.<br/> <br/>After reading your comments, perhaps there were better images to be had of some mares <i>with</i> foals, but who knows.</td>', 'In response to your request for comments. I gave this a 4.  Quite a nice capture with her eyes and the mane / hair blowing in the wind.  Depending what you had to work with, perhaps a variation in cropping, including a nudge rotate up on the right to straighten.  The centered composition isn''t as strong as something off-centered may have been in my opinion, but again, depends what you had to work with.  The tone itself perhaps a little strong (especially on the pink side) but that could be intentional.  A variation in the hue/tone may have brought out more features as well.  Overall the focus seems a bit soft, but could be a result of the pp. After reading your comments, perhaps there were better images to be had of some mares with foals, but who knows.', '2008-05-08 08:59:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(4689837, 674507, 69008, '<td valign="top">I see that you are new here at DPC, so first, welcome to the digital madness.  This is a nice night shot  and a good score for your first challenge entry. A couple of things have been mentioned that could be improved. The first thing that I noticed being a little off, is the camera moved a bit, which may be because of wind, or just not a stable enough place to keep the camera still.  I see that you were at a restaurant, which explains that you didn''t have a tripod in your pocket LOL..  <br/>I have found that about 6 to 10 sec, and about f 5.6 or 8 works great for lightning shots at night. <br/>Keep shooting and have fun with the new XTi. <br/> <br/></td>', 'I see that you are new here at DPC, so first, welcome to the digital madness.  This is a nice night shot  and a good score for your first challenge entry. A couple of things have been mentioned that could be improved. The first thing that I noticed being a little off, is the camera moved a bit, which may be because of wind, or just not a stable enough place to keep the camera still.  I see that you were at a restaurant, which explains that you didn''t have a tripod in your pocket LOL..  I have found that about 6 to 10 sec, and about f 5.6 or 8 works great for lightning shots at night. Keep shooting and have fun with the new XTi.  ', '2008-05-08 09:03:00.000000', NULL, 0),
