(4696243, 673439, 68035, '<td valign="top">Simply breathtaking Karen and very well derving of the 7th place<br/> <br/>I love the contrast between the sharpness of the shot and the dreaminess that sepia can give<br/> <br/>There is a sense of tranquility and timelessness about this image, it is as if the whole world has stopped and this is the only thing that remains<br/> <br/>I love it</td>', 'Simply breathtaking Karen and very well derving of the 7th place I love the contrast between the sharpness of the shot and the dreaminess that sepia can give There is a sense of tranquility and timelessness about this image, it is as if the whole world has stopped and this is the only thing that remains I love it', '2008-05-12 06:54:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(4696874, 674504, 67697, '<td valign="top">I didn''t vote on this but would have given this a 7.  The brown tone is perfect for this prairie look.  I love the bokeh and having the one flower in focus is perfect.</td>', 'I didn''t vote on this but would have given this a 7.  The brown tone is perfect for this prairie look.  I love the bokeh and having the one flower in focus is perfect.', '2008-05-12 11:12:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(4699553, 673588, 55956, '<td valign="top">Greeting from Critique Club<br/> <br/>Hi, I think that is a good photograph. From compositional point of view I would more space on the right. The people on the background, on the right side, is a bit distracting but probably could be used as compositional element if the cropped girls on the right would be entire(with a bit of more blur on the background). I like the pose of the models and I would that be a candid photo. the sepia tone work well in this photo.<br/> <br/>For any question about this comment please contact me.<br/> <br/>Gennaro</td>', 'Greeting from Critique Club Hi, I think that is a good photograph. From compositional point of view I would more space on the right. The people on the background, on the right side, is a bit distracting but probably could be used as compositional element if the cropped girls on the right would be entire(with a bit of more blur on the background). I like the pose of the models and I would that be a candid photo. the sepia tone work well in this photo. For any question about this comment please contact me. Gennaro', '2008-05-13 15:41:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(4699648, 673306, 55956, '<td valign="top">Greeting from critique club.<br/> <br/>Hi, I see that you have a very low score for this image. most of the comments that you have are true. the composition isn''t really interesting, the main flower isn''t sharp and the focus is a bit far from it. the image don''t seems a good image for sepia challenge, probably you could improve it with shadows and highlight, I read that you have used the camera settings for the sepia tuning probably a conversion with photoshop or other image editor should be more helpful.<br/> <br/>for any question about this comment please contact me.<br/> <br/>gennaro</td>', 'Greeting from critique club. Hi, I see that you have a very low score for this image. most of the comments that you have are true. the composition isn''t really interesting, the main flower isn''t sharp and the focus is a bit far from it. the image don''t seems a good image for sepia challenge, probably you could improve it with shadows and highlight, I read that you have used the camera settings for the sepia tuning probably a conversion with photoshop or other image editor should be more helpful. for any question about this comment please contact me. gennaro', '2008-05-13 16:19:23.000000', NULL, 0),
